-- the vestibule of EVERYONE IS HERE: the disagreements between the product as its team describes it
-- and the treaty as it stands, each a statement in the assay's own terms and the darkness it waits on.
-- a held statement seats when what it waits on arrives: the customer's word, a carrier, a reach of the
-- drawer's fragment, or a seating in the treaty's translator. read by bin/counter book.
-- the first round (2026-09-04, Abe's answers through isaac) seated six statements into the assay
-- (the_audience_hears_the_receipt_by_name, outside_the_audience_hears_no_receipt, the_sender_is_never_asked,
-- the_same_page_counts_only_within_earshot, the_payer_is_the_owner_or_the_host, edit_is_within_sight and
-- its two instances), refuted one (a member is a Membership; guests are never members; who can be asked is
-- the audience of the channel minus the sender), and left these.

-- held (waiting on: a carrier and the translator. the room's confirmed field and the turnstile everyone members confirmed are at the wrong grain: a confirmation lives in the channel its request was sent in, heard by that channel's audience. Request carries it now; Room still carries the old list, and the treaty's translator seats Room's columns by hand.)
theorem the_rooms_receipt_is_its_requests (r : Room) (qs : List Request) :
    r.confirmed = joinMap (fun q => q.confirmed) qs := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: a carrier and the translator. a member is a Membership — a name and a role in the room's planning team; guests are parties, never members; a channel's audience is a list of members. the assay has no roster.)
theorem an_audience_is_members (q : Request) (roster : List Nat) (m : Nat) (hm : m ∈ q.audience) : m ∈ roster := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: a probe and the translator. the Vendor Room is confirmed as the bach lane's shape — nothing posted there reaches any couple-facing surface, aggregates included (the_same_page_counts_only_within_earshot). one more Ask, the couple's seat without it; the translator names the six asks by hand.)
theorem the_vendor_room_wall (r : Room) (v : List Nat) (hv : v ≠ r.bach) :
    reads roomFace coupleSeat (withBach r v) = reads roomFace coupleSeat r := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: the drawer's fragment. a face parameterized by a vendor's id — vendorFace v, the .mine reading — is proved (a_vendor_never_sees_anothers_invoice), confirmed exactly (the planner and the venue are vendors for invoices; hosting adds nothing; the couple sees all), and not drawn. budget lines are couple-only: a probe the assay lacks.)
theorem a_vendor_sees_only_their_own (v : Nat) (r : Room) :
    (vendorFace v).obs r .mine = (r.ledger.filter (fun e => Nat.beq e.1 v)).map (·.2.2) := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: the drawer's fragment. a def over an enum (pays, joinsFree, sees, edits, owner) is skipped as a def over a kind; each is one CASE expression or one lookup table. confirmed without exception, door two included.)
theorem the_pricing_rule_is_two_lines : (∀ ρ, joinsFree ρ = true) ∧ pays .party = false ∧ pays .couple = true := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: the customer's word on two "today"s. the day-of sheet and tasks are edit-by-all in the demo; and the venue sees the guest list today because the list view is gated on edit rights. the assay states the recommended change (the_venue_edits_the_floor_and_never_sees_the_list); the demo does not yet.)
theorem the_day_of_sheet_has_an_editor (ρ : Role) : edits ρ .dayOf = true := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: the treaty's translator. the row, in the customer's words: a file attached in the Vendor room; the couple's Files page; expected absent. visible is proved and drawn; a Channel and a File have no seating in the replay.)
theorem a_vendor_room_file_is_absent_from_the_couples_files (f : File) (couple : Nat)
    (h : ¬ couple ∈ f.channel.audience) : ¬ visible f couple := sorry
-- end

-- held (waiting on: the product that spans rooms. My season is confirmed as a seat over many rooms: nobody but the vendor sees it, nothing on it exceeds the vendor's slice of each room, and one aggregate is allowed — what they are owed and what they have been paid, summed over their own invoices. the next diagonal, Face at a list of rooms.)
theorem a_season_is_a_seat_over_many_rooms (rs : List Room) (v : Nat) :
    (rs.map (fun r => (vendorFace v).obs r .mine)).length = rs.length := sorry
-- end
